 "stimulus_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\">\n  <li>The height of a baseball, in feet, is modeled by the function <span data-math=\"h\">h</span> given by the equation <span data-math=\"h(t)=3+60t-16t^2\">h(t)=3+60t-16t^2</span>. The graph of the function is shown.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img alt=\"A curve on a graph, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis, time, seconds, scale 0 to 8, by 1’s. Vertical axis, height, feet, scale 0 to 200, by 20’s. A curve passes through the points 0 comma 3, 2 comma 59, and 3 comma 36.\" height=\"213\" src=\"exercises/media/2e5589acff74a1f9.svg\" width=\"315\"></p>",
